    "q-84594": {
      "dom_id": "step-q84594",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=-8,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=6,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=0$ are eigenvalues, and \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. Find the matrices $P$ and $D$ such that $PD{P}^{-1}=A,$ where $D$ is a diagonal matrix.",
      "worked_solution": "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-8,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=6,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=0,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-8,$\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=6,$ and\n\n- the $3$rd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{3}=0.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-84594-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$",
